```tsx
type SideNavProps = {
  nav: NavItem[];
  className?: string;
  variant?: "board" | "paper";
  onNavigate?: () => void;
};
```
- Destructure `onNavigate` in the component signature.
- On the `<Link ...>` inside the map, add `onClick={onNavigate}` (keep everything else, including `aria-current`).

## Edit 5: src/components/shell/app-shell.tsx
- Add import: `import { MobileNav } from "@/components/shell/mobile-nav";` (group with the other `@/components/shell` imports, alphabetically after locked-empty-state import if present; current imports are Seal/Wordmark from marketing/wordmark, SignOutButton, SideNav — place MobileNav import so the list stays alphabetically sorted: mobile-nav comes after marketing/wordmark and before sign-out-button).
- Delete the entire `<details className="group relative">...</details>` block (the hamburger summary + dropdown, roughly lines 47-67) and replace it with `<MobileNav roleLabel={roleLabel(role)} nav={nav} />`. The dropdown previously positioned absolute inside the details; the header is `sticky` so absolute positioning still anchors to the header — no wrapper changes needed.
- Change `text-primary-foreground/50` in the sidebar "panel" label paragraph (line ~32) to `text-primary-foreground/65` (contrast fix on the chalkboard sidebar).
- Keep the SignOutButton import (still used by the desktop sidebar).

## Edit 6: src/app/(student)/student/check-in/check-in-panel.tsx
Distinguish "browser can't scan QR" from "camera unavailable" copy:
- Add below the existing `type CameraState` declaration:
```tsx
type CameraUnavailableReason = "scanner_unsupported" | "camera_unavailable";
```
- Add state next to `cameraState`: `const [unavailableReason, setUnavailableReason] = useState<CameraUnavailableReason | null>(null);`
- In the scanner effect, where it currently does:
```tsx
if (!DetectorCtor || !navigator.mediaDevices) {
  setCameraState("unavailable");
  return;
}
```
also add `setUnavailableReason("scanner_unsupported");` before the return.
- In the `.catch(() => { if (!cancelled) setCameraState("unavailable"); })` at the end of the getUserMedia chain, also call `setUnavailableReason("camera_unsupported" === "x" ? "camera_unavailable" : "camera_unavailable")` — NO, simply: change that catch to:
```tsx
.catch(() => {
  if (!cancelled) {
    setUnavailableReason("camera_unavailable");
    setCameraState("unavailable");
  }
});
```
- Replace the unavailable message JSX:
```tsx
{cameraState === "unavailable" ? (
  <p className="text-muted-foreground rounded-lg border border-dashed p-4 text-sm">
    Camera is unavailable on this device — paste the check-in code instead.
  </p>
) : (
```
with:
```tsx
{cameraState === "unavailable" ? (
  <p className="text-muted-foreground rounded-lg border border-dashed p-4 text-sm">
    {unavailableReason === "scanner_unsupported"
      ? "QR scanning isn't supported in this browser — paste the check-in code below instead."
      : "Camera is unavailable on this device — paste the check-in code below instead."}
  </p>
) : (
```

